Max total gcd Sum m = 6, i.e. min defect 14 - 6 = 8 [COMPUTED, numerical].

Sum m = 7 search, all with 0 non-degenerate solutions:
- 13/13 gcd patterns x 30k starts (Lucas-point model);
- 397/397 incidence structures with explicit Lucas-node sharing x 10k starts (node model, out/node7.log; node7_hits.txt is empty);
- inside the FSP locus: 4 extension types x 4k starts;
- on the reflection-symmetric locus: 5 Sum m = 8 patterns x 20k starts each (Sum m = 7 is impossible there by parity).

Sum m = 6 points, all 0-dimensional by slice test:
- FSP + f_1 full: 65 found, Lincoln-Petersen estimate 66; 8 real in one run;
- FSP + extra Lucas point of one cubic member: 220 found, estimate 239; 14 real;
- symmetric (2,1,1,1,1): 170 hits / 20k, at least 28 distinct points, 6 real;
- symmetric (2,2,2,0,0): 74 hits; (0,2,2,1,1): 22 hits; (0,3,3,0,0): 1 complex point with two Lucas-full cubics.
- None of the ~285 FSP points has a 7th incidence: the closest non-Lucas residual is 5e-3, where a true incidence would be ~1e-12.

Field test: the real minimisers were refined to 49-58 digits. No invariant (c, l_j r_j, r_i r_j; or T, u_i for FSP points) satisfies a polynomial of degree <= 8-12 with coefficients <= 1e12-1e15.

Calibration on k = 3 (reproduces E3): rho-family [2,1,1] at dim 1, P23 [0,2,2] at dim 0, and 0 hits for Sum m = 5 (3k starts per pattern).

Recall caveat: the plain gcd-pattern survey found 0 of the ~239 FSP+1 points in pattern (1,2,1,1,1). Hit rates: node model on FSP structures 3.5-5%; symmetric excess points 0.1-0.9%.

Exact timing failures:
- Korselt ideal std in 9 variables over F_32003: > 300 s;
- FSP locus (5 variables, two formulations): > 3000 s and > 900 s;
- symmetric Sum m = 8 system (6 variables, 7 equations) mod 1000003: > 900 s.

Relative defect: 8/14 = 0.571, versus 0.5 for the k = 3 rho-family.
